course: dictionary
lesson: 12605
title: Formal words and what they mean
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to letters, labels and news reports rather than to everyday talk. Discontinuation is one of them. It means stopping something that used to go on, on purpose. «The shop announced the discontinuation of its blue bicycles.» Here the shop has stopped selling the blue bicycles.
explain: The verb is discontinue. «The bus company will discontinue the number 9 route in May.» The clues are «will», «in May» and the idea of a route being stopped. So discontinue means stop, and discontinuation is the act of stopping.
explain: Ordinary people would say «they stopped making it». Try your simple meaning in the sentence: «The shop announced the stopping of its blue bicycles» sounds clumsy, so the formal word is a label for a bigger, official ending. When you read it on a label or in a letter, swap in «stopped» to check.
fact: Discontinuation is a noun. The verb is discontinue.
fact: «Discontinuation» means stopping something that used to continue, usually on purpose.
fact: It is used for products, services, bus routes and medicines.
fact: Common phrases: discontinuation of a product, discontinuation of a service.
fact: It is a formal word, so you will see it in official letters, on labels and in news reports, and people in everyday talk usually say «stopped» instead.
exercise: «The discontinuation of the old phone made many fans sad.» What does discontinuation mean here? | Buying the phone for a friend | *Stopping the phone being made | Charging the phone every night | Making the phone bigger and faster
exercise: Which word means the same as discontinue? | *stop | repeat | upgrade | start
exercise: Which sentence uses discontinuation correctly? | I had a discontinuation for my lunch today. | The discontinuation was a fast red dog. | Discontinuation is my favourite colour. | *The company announced the discontinuation of its old tablets.
test: «The council confirmed the discontinuation of the Saturday bus service.» What does this tell us? | The Saturday bus will now run twice as often | The bus is now free for everyone | The bus driver has a new uniform | *The Saturday bus will no longer run
test: Which word is the verb form of discontinuation? | continue | *discontinue | discount | disconnect
exam: A label on a box says «This item has been discontinued.» What does it tell a shopper? | It is on sale this weekend only | *It is no longer made or sold | It is free to take home today | It has just been made by a new company
